# Normalised Hahn-series embeddings induce places of F_N

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.exists_place_of_emb` (`78e864be-091d-51f3-b418-323cd2bbb50e`), by
Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `aa026c6d-f9d9-5692-a82a-9066f00dedf5`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $N$ be a non-zero natural number and let $j_0$ be an element of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$
(realised as `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`). Write $\overline{F_N}$ for `modularFunctionFieldBar N`, the
intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ over
$\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the image, under the coefficient-extension embedding
`coeffEmb`, of `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, itself the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over
$\mathbb{Q}$ by the family `divisorExpansions N`. Let $\psi$ be an element of `Emb N j₀`, that is, a
pair consisting of an $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra homomorphism $\psi_1$ from $\overline{F_N}$
into the field `HahnSeries ℚ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` of Hahn series with rational exponents and
coefficients in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, together with the normalisation that $\psi_1$ sends `jBar
N` (the image of the $q$-expansion of $j$) to $j_0 + q$, i.e. to the constant series $j_0$ plus the
monomial of exponent $1$ and coefficient $1$. The assertion is that there exist a place $w$ of
$\overline{F_N}$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ — a valuation subring of $\overline{F_N}$ containing
$\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, distinct from the whole field, and a principal ideal ring — and a rational
number $g > 0$ such that for every $x \in \overline{F_N}$ one has $(\operatorname{ord}_w x)\, g =
\operatorname{order}(\psi_1 x)$, where $\operatorname{ord}_w x$ is the integer $-\log$ of the adic
valuation of $x$ at $w$ and $\operatorname{order}$ is the exponent of the leading term of a Hahn
series.

This is the step that converts a normalised Hahn-series expansion of the level $N$ modular function
field at $j_0$ into a genuine place of that field, with the orders of vanishing matching up to a
single positive rational factor (the reciprocal of the ramification index over $j_0$). It is used in
the counting of places where `jBar` has order one, in
[`ModularCurve.card_filter_ord_jBar_eq_one_eq_nuThree`]
(thm.html#ModularCurve.card_filter_ord_jBar_eq_one_eq_nuThree)
and
[`ModularCurve.card_filter_ord_jBar_sub_1728_eq_one_eq_nuTwo`]
(thm.html#ModularCurve.card_filter_ord_jBar_sub_1728_eq_one_eq_nuTwo),
and in [`ModularCurve.emd_holds`](thm.html#ModularCurve.emd_holds).

